+Read-only analysis reuse. Each readonly producer above (the database-input
+driver of the OriginalReadonlyReferenceDocument owner, the Fresh seed of
+Pending, Salsa and no-handle sources, and the structure-only coarse-token
+driver) is the configured FreshAnalysisDriver, a pure function of its complete
+input: the source text, dialect, the configuration values the driver was built
+from (disabled codes, non-ASCII mode, extra commands, pack key and resource
+inputs), the published class-factory allocation, the analyser path, any
+supplied document analysis input, the structure-only selection, the candidate
+sidecar stubs in the document's ancestor directories, the analyser-input
+epoch, the factory generation and the URI publication generation. The
+backend's ReadonlyAnalysisMemo returns a stored run only when that whole input
+is equal, and otherwise runs the driver exactly as before; a run whose own
+input names a sidecar outside the probed candidates is not retained. A hit
+replaces only
+the producer call: the request's path receipt is checked as a run would check
+it, and every capture, snapshot and final-transaction predicate in this
+section still runs on the request's own captured state. The memo holds no
+database snapshot, never enters the Salsa memo or its LRU, and does its
+lookup, run and insertion on the request's own blocking worker. Open documents
+keep one entry per URI and purpose. Closed documents, and an open document's
+entries once it closes, share a least-recently-used tier bounded by entry
+count and estimated bytes (`ReadonlyAnalysisMemoLimits`, by default 256
+entries and 512 MiB, applied to an estimate of each analysis's size). This
+closed tier is the one exception to deep analysis state being an open-document
+cost: it holds read-only fresh analyses only and never warms the Salsa deep
+tier. The tier an entry joins comes from the memo's own open set, which
+`didOpen` and `didClose` maintain, not from the request's earlier snapshot.
+Process-global registry state the driver reads (pack and spec reloads and the
+core surface generation behind the context-registry cache) changes only under
+the analyser-input gate, which advances the analyser-input epoch; the epoch is
+part of the key, and advancing it clears the memo and refuses runs from
+earlier epochs, so no superseded registry or factory generation is retained.
+Sidecar stubs are probed by exact name (the dialect and the analyser and unit
+profile names of its environment and of any supplied input) in every ancestor
+directory, recording what the analyser's lookups observe: whether the
+candidate is a file and its UTF-8 content. Retired URIs leave the memo through
+`forget_uri_states`.
+
