 so a cross-file read cannot retain every file it ever touched.
 
+The one bounded exception is the read-only analysis memo
+(`readonly_analysis_memo.rs`). Read-only requests (workspace symbols, reference
+reports, call hierarchy, logical lenses, coarse semantic tokens) reuse their
+fresh-driver analysis, together with the source text it was keyed on. Open
+documents keep one entry per URI and purpose. Closed documents share a
+least-recently-used tier bounded by entry count and estimated bytes
+(`ReadonlyAnalysisMemoLimits`, by default 256 entries and 512 MiB). The byte
+bound applies to an estimate (64 bytes per source byte plus 16 KiB per
+entry), not to measured allocations. Only entries of the current
+analyser-input epoch and class-factory generation are kept, so a superseded
+registry or factory generation is released when the epoch moves rather than
+outliving the bound. The memo never enters the Salsa deep tier, and a
+workspace-symbol request touching more closed files than the entry bound gets
+no reuse across requests.
